---
// C批：食品级/卫生级
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CtaBand from '../../components/CtaBand.astro';

const title = 'Food-Grade Peristaltic Pumps: Hygienic Transfer Without the Cleanup';
const date = 'August 25, 2026';
const readTime = '9 min read';
const related = [
  { href: '/blog/laboratory-peristaltic-pump-guide/', title: 'Lab Peristaltic Pump Guide', readTime: '10 min read' },
  { href: '/blog/peristaltic-pump-tubing-guide/', title: 'Peristaltic Pump Tubing Guide', readTime: '12 min read' },
  { href: '/blog/peristaltic-vs-diaphragm-pump/', title: 'Peristaltic vs Diaphragm Pump', readTime: '10 min read' },
];
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} | PERIFLOW Blog`}
  description="Why food processors choose peristaltic pumps — hygienic design, gentle transfer, easy CIP — and how to spec food-grade tubing and pump heads."
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="bg-navy-950 text-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:py-20">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm text-slate-400" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/" class="transition hover:text-white">Home</a>
        <span class="mx-1">/</span>
        <a href="/blog/" class="transition hover:text-white">Blog</a>
        <span class="mx-1">/</span>
        <span class="text-slate-200">Food-Grade Pump Guide</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="max-w-4xl text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">{title}</h1>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2 text-sm text-slate-400">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="grid h-8 w-8 place-items-center rounded-full bg-brand-blue text-sm font-bold text-white">RC</span>
          Ray Chan
        </span>
        <span>·</span>
        <span>{date}</span>
        <span>·</span>
        <span>{readTime}</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 正文 -->
  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:py-16">
      <article class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-headings:font-extrabold prose-headings:text-navy-950 prose-h2:mt-12 prose-h3:mt-8 prose-a:text-brand-blue">

        <p>
          In food processing, the two questions that decide a pump purchase are: does it contaminate the product, and is it worth cleaning afterwards? Peristaltic pumps answer both with the same feature — the product only touches the inside of a disposable tube. No mechanical seals to harbor bacteria, no dead zones, no product trapped in rotor cavities.
        </p>

        <h2 id="why">Why Food Lines Choose Peristaltic</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Hygienic by design.</strong> The fluid path is a single smooth tube. Clean it, autoclave it or throw it away — the pump head never touches the product.</li>
          <li><strong>Gentle transfer.</strong> Low-shear pumping preserves texture in sauces, batters, purees and dairy — no emulsification, no aeration.</li>
          <li><strong>Handles particulates.</strong> Chunky products (soups, fruit fillings, pet food) pass through without damage because there are no impellers to break them.</li>
          <li><strong>Dry-run tolerant.</strong> A hopper that runs empty will not burn out the pump — the tube just keeps rolling.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="tubing">Food-Grade Tubing: What to Ask For</h2>
        <p>
          The tube is the food-contact surface, so its certification matters. For food and beverage service, specify:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Platinum-cured silicone</strong> — the default for food contact; low extractables, transparent, autoclavable. Check FDA 21 CFR 177.2600 compliance for direct food contact.</li>
          <li><strong>Norprene-type TPE</strong> — longer life for continuous transfer and pump-and-fill duty; good chemical and temperature tolerance.</li>
          <li><strong>EPDM</strong> — for hot water CIP lines and fatty products where silicone degrades.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Always request the compliance documentation (FDA / EU 1935/2004) with your order — your quality team will ask for it at audit time anyway.
        </p>

        <h2 id="faq">FAQ</h2>
        <h3>Can peristaltic pumps handle CIP/SIP?</h3>
        <p>Yes — the tubing can be cleaned in place with hot water or steam, or replaced with a sterile spare. For SIP, use a tube rated for steam exposure and confirm the autoclave cycle with the manufacturer.</p>
        <h3>What flow rates are typical for food filling lines?</h3>
        <p>Filling lines commonly run 0.5–12 L/min per head. A YZ35 head with 82# tubing reaches 12,000 ml/min at 600 rpm; multi-channel YZ15 heads handle lower-volume multi-line filling.</p>
        <h3>Is the pump head itself food-contact rated?</h3>
        <p>The head does not contact the product, so it does not need food-grade certification — but it should be washdown-friendly (stainless or sealed housing) for hygiene in the production area.</p>
      </article>

      <!-- Related 互链 -->
      <div class="mt-12 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-8">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-brand-blue">Related Reading</p>
        <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
          {related.map((r) => (
            <a href={r.href} class="group block rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 transition hover:border-brand-blue">
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold leading-snug text-navy-950 transition group-hover:text-brand-blue">{r.title}</p>
              <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-slate-400">{r.readTime}</p>
            </a>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-slate-500">
          Explore our <a href="/products/pump-heads/" class="font-semibold text-brand-blue hover:underline">pump heads</a> and <a href="/products/tubing/" class="font-semibold text-brand-blue hover:underline">pump tubing</a> for factory-direct pricing.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    title="Spec a Food-Grade Pump for Your Line?"
    subtitle="Tell us the product, flow and CIP requirements — we recommend head, drive and certified tubing within 24 hours."
  />
</Layout>
